## `ECR-D-014`, after five independent rounds

Round 1 cleared `ECR-D-006` and refused this. Round 2 found the ruling **enforced by nothing**
— a mutation skipping the cap check on the canonical path survived all 846 tests while the
build wrote a 249-token prefix against a cap of 200. Round 3 declared the enforcement condition
**fully discharged** against fifteen mutations and said it must not be re-audited. Round 4
re-proved the substance and refused on record accuracy. **Round 5 re-proved it again and
recommended closure**, choosing option (c) — close with named residuals — of three it was asked
to weigh.

**The closing act is a `qa-engineer`'s, in a distinct cold session, and this entry only records
it.** LAW-02 clause 5 and LAW-05 are satisfied on their own terms: **no session that repaired
this ECR certified its own repair, across four consecutive attempts.**

**What the closure does not say.** It does not find those repairs clean. Each of the four
introduced a defect of the class it was repairing — a count asserted rather than measured, a
coverage claim wider than its coverage, a half-replaced sentence, and twice a check that did
not catch what it was written for. **That is a process finding and it belongs to `OI-V-17`**,
not to an ECR about a token cap. Holding this one open a sixth time would have made it the
carrier for a class it does not own, and would not have reached the cause.

## The check, rebuilt by giving up on phrasings

Round 5 got **twelve of thirteen** sequence phrasings past the previous rule, including
`last_ledger_seq: 2` — the field's own name — because there is no word boundary after an
underscore. Matching the *forms* a value takes is unwinnable: catch `seq 2` and lose to "the
second entry"; catch both and lose to "entry two".

So the rule no longer matches forms. **A section named for a governed field may contain no
numeral and no written number at all.** Re-measured against the round's own list: **13 of 13
and 8 of 8 caught**, every section hole closed, the fenced-YAML case closed, and both converse
properties intact — a blockquote recounting the defect does not fire, and the findings register
stays out of scope, because a rule that cannot tell *"X is current"* from *"X was wrongly
called current"* is a trap for the honest.

